## Brand Story (short)
Deplora started because modern teams were forced to choose between expensive hosted LLM services and painful self-hosting. Founders saw engineering teams spending weeks on ops, wrestling with rate limits, and losing control of sensitive data. Deplora was born to remove the friction: provide a developer-first platform that provisions and runs open-source LLMs with predictable pricing, in your preferred region, and with a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Our early customers are platform engineers and ML teams who want control without the operational drag — and the product was built from that need.

---

## Manifesto (for culture & comms)
We believe infrastructure should be invisible.  
We believe teams should control their models, their data, and their costs.  
We believe developer experience matters — beautiful tools ship better products.  
We believe transparency beats surprises: predictable pricing, clear SLAs, honest limits.  
We build tools that let engineers focus on product, not servers.  
— That’s Deplora.

---

## Quick Usage Rules (copy for team)
- Use Logo Blue (`text-blue-600`) for Deplora wordmark and primary icons
- Use gradient primaries (`from-blue-600 to-purple-600`) for main CTAs only  
- Use semantic colors consistently for status badges and alerts
- Keep microcopy short; default to helpful next-step guidance  
- When in doubt, prefer clarity and simplicity

